PREAMBLE

Zengram Lite is a WebAssembly build of the Zengram agentic-memory framework
over the Zeta database engine, intended to run in a web browser (or a WASI
host). It is free to use — including for commercial purposes — at no charge. It
is not open source: the framework and engine source code are not included in
this distribution, and a few narrow restrictions apply (see RESTRICTIONS
below).

This license covers the compiled Zengram Lite artifact and the hand-authored
materials distributed with it — not the source code of the framework or engine.
The Zengram framework source is planned for separate release as open source
under the Apache License 2.0 (publication pending); the Zeta engine source
remains closed and is available only to parties under a separate Non-Disclosure
Agreement and arrangement. Whichever the status of that source, the compiled
artifact is distributed under this license, and nothing here grants access to
engine source or governs the framework's separate open-source release.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

